  partName: Left Front Sensor
  description: The Left Front Sensor is a small, complex-shaped device positioned
    at the top-left-front of the engine, constructed from Material.001, responsible
    for monitoring critical engine parameters such as air/fuel mixture, engine speed,
    or coolant temperature. This sensor provides essential data to the engine control
    unit, enabling optimal engine performance, efficiency, and emissions control.
    One interesting aspect of the Left Front Sensor is its ability to adapt to changing
    engine conditions, ensuring accurate readings and reliable engine operation.
